"""Explicit evidence/experiment protocol for all three official tasks."""
import json,re
PROMPT='''You run a CPU industrial-model experiment loop. A is six-class gas classification (maximize Macro-F1), B is bearing RUL in minutes (minimize RMSE), C is engine RUL in cycles (minimize RMSE). Start from the supplied official checkpoint. You have at most ten experiment attempts and twenty-one model calls including optional inspections and final review. Read the supplied evidence and training code, form a falsifiable explanation, run one experiment, and revise the explanation using the actual receipt. Historical hypotheses are unverified interpretations. Lower overall error alone does not prove the proposed cause. Bias is prediction minus target. Report group tradeoffs. All data are repeatedly used public development data, not independent test evidence.
Every experiment uses operation core_code and explicitly submits exactly five pure numerical Python functions (plan,learning_rate,sample_weights,batch_order,loss). The selected core is always continued first on source data using inherited Adam; successful candidates must increase optimizer steps. An optional supplement is either {"kind":"steady_head"} for A or {"kind":"residual_trees","trees":80,"learning_rate":0.05} for C. No other operation or implicit/default program is available. steady_head uses the unchanged fixed source-only fitting recipe once; an existing fitted head cannot be refit. residual_trees uses the unchanged algorithm and appends 1..80 trees at learning_rate1e-6..1; it retains the old forest and learns the residual of this trial's updated core plus that forest. Omitting supplement preserves existing head/forest without fitting. After these operations and any optional A readout, the fixed evaluator evaluates and accepts the entire candidate only for strict main-metric improvement, once in the same trial. Rejection or failure preserves the entire selected parent and consumes one attempt. No separate intermediate adoption or free supplement round. Tree iterations are not epochs. Do not confuse training normalization with displayed units. For classification, loss takes raw logits and integer labels and must return the derivative with respect to logits. For regression, loss takes normalized scalar predictions/targets. The regression reference program uses explicit uniform row weights. Regression groups is None; device metadata is not a required training input and device-level diagnostics are unavailable. Do not infer or fabricate device groups. C residual fits use the submitted sample-weight function when groups is None.
For A only, core_code may additionally include readout_expression as a complete nonempty string. program remains mandatory. The submitted program continues the selected core once using source training data and inherited Adam; any explicit supplement fits next, and the optional expression then replaces the single readout on that updated core/head. If omitted, retain the selected expression. Evaluate and adopt this whole candidate once in the same trial. No standalone/free readout operation. An existing fitted head and normalization remain unchanged. Readout expressions run per row with readonly raw(128), x(128, inherited normalization/clipping), hidden(32), logits(6 raw core outputs), base_prob(6 upstream probabilities including any existing head, before readout), classes(6 integer indices in checkpoint order). base_prob denotes the SAME continued upstream, not the pre-training parent. Return six finite nonnegative real weights with at least one positive; normalize as weights/max then divide by sum, preserving zeros. No labels, IDs, metadata, history, distinguished pair, state or I/O. Expressions allow numerical literals, these names, lists/tuples, indexing/slices, arithmetic + - * / ** & |, unary operators and single comparisons, and np.abs square sqrt log1p exp tanh sin cos minimum maximum clip where mean std sum max min argmax concatenate stack with axis/keepdims keywords only. Limits:1800 characters,400 AST nodes,256 sequence items,4096 intermediate elements,ndim<=2,literal magnitude<=10000,exponent magnitude<=8; nonfinite intermediates fail. A may inspect readout_summary for per-class p10/p50/p90 of selected-parent logits, upstream and selected probabilities. These are pre-training diagnostics, not post-update candidate results. There is no supplied repair formula; changes must be tested. A joint gain alone does not identify readout as its cause.
Core programs may use NumPy vector expressions, assignments, if/return, tuples/dicts, and the listed numerical functions. Within sample_weights only, [value for c in range(6)] may enumerate the six class indices, with one local index, no filters and no nesting. Other iteration is forbidden. No imports, I/O, private attributes, input mutation or dynamic calls. Array methods are not allowed calls; use only listed np functions or listed builtins, in their displayed call forms. plan returns epochs1..5 and batch_size16..4096; max1500 optimizer updates per experiment. Learning rate1e-6..0.1. A wrong gradient or invalid program is a failed attempt, not a free retry. Prefer one interpretable change. The reference recipes are explicit priors, not experiments already performed in this run; joint A/C continuation differs from historical standalone fitting and has unverified scores; do not cite them as current results. You may retain or challenge them with an explicit test.
Return exactly one bare JSON object. No Markdown code fences (including ```json), surrounding explanation, or other text:
{"tool":"experiment","reflection":"what the most recent receipt supports and does not support","proposal":{"operation":"core_code","hypothesis":"...","expected_result":"...","falsifier":"...","program":"the complete five functions"}}
For a supplement retain operation=core_code and the complete program, and add the optional supplement object described above. Every proposal retains hypothesis/expected_result/falsifier. B supports core_code without a supplement or readout.
Optional inspections: {"tool":"read","resource":"training_code|current_program|baseline_program|history|trial/N/proposal|trial/N/report"} or {"tool":"analyze","dataset":"train|selection","view":"group_errors|target_bins|feature_error_correlation|readout_summary"}. At most one inspection is allowed before each experiment; then you must experiment. Current group metrics, source, training counts and history are already provided; inspect only if needed. Classification target_bins is unavailable. Resource N must already be completed.
Tool results use one canonical body: a current_tool_results entry contains either result or result_ref. result_ref is a JSON Pointer to a top-level field in this same request, for example /history means the complete history field is the tool result. Read that referenced value as the full result, not a summary or missing evidence. References are emitted only for exactly equal read results; unshared results stay inline. The original tool result is preserved in its on-disk receipt.
After ten attempts, return {"tool":"finish","conclusion":"...","supported":["..."],"not_supported":["..."]}. Never finish early. Do not repeat unsuccessful identical experiments without a justified changed condition. Keep explanations concise. Do not claim local optimality, causal identification, hidden generalization or historical self-improvement without evidence.
'''
NUMERICAL_FUNCTIONS='array asarray ones zeros ones_like zeros_like full_like arange abs maximum minimum clip where mean sum std median quantile percentile exp log log1p max sqrt square power tanh sin cos sign bincount unique argsort sort concatenate stack repeat tile reshape isfinite all any; np.pi; len float int min max abs sum; array.shape; bare loss operators: weighted_cross_entropy(pred,target,weights,gamma=0), weighted_mse(pred,target,weights), weighted_huber(pred,target,weights,delta)'
REFERENCE_RECIPES={
'A':'Joint-rule prior, not a verified score:10 one-epoch core candidates, batch32, initial LR0.01, halve after rejection; on candidate10 add supplement kind=steady_head after core continuation. No standalone head round.',
'B':'Current metadata-independent rule, not a carried-over historical score:one epoch,batch64,uniform row weights; same-parent LR sequence0.006,0.012,0.003,0.0015,... excluding attempted rates; ten candidates.',
'C':'Joint-rule prior, not a verified score:each of10 candidates explicitly continues core one epoch,batch256,LR0.0005,explicit row weights; then supplement appends80 residual trees,15 leaves,min_leaf30,explicit row weights,tree LR initially0.05 and halved after rejection. Core changes before residual fitting; historical scores do not carry over.'}


def parse(text):
    def unique(pairs):
        result={}
        for k,v in pairs:
            if k in result:raise ValueError('Duplicate JSON field')
            result[k]=v
        return result
    payload=text.strip()
    def reject_constant(value):raise ValueError('Nonfinite JSON constant')
    d=json.loads(payload,object_pairs_hook=unique,parse_constant=reject_constant)
    fields={'experiment':{'tool','reflection','proposal'},'read':{'tool','resource'},'analyze':{'tool','dataset','view'},'finish':{'tool','conclusion','supported','not_supported'}}
    if not isinstance(d,dict) or d.get('tool') not in fields or set(d)!=fields[d['tool']]:raise ValueError('Tool schema mismatch')
    if d['tool']=='experiment' and (not isinstance(d['proposal'],dict) or not isinstance(d['reflection'],str)):raise ValueError('Invalid experiment object')
    if d['tool']=='read' and (not isinstance(d['resource'],str) or d['resource'] not in ('training_code','current_program','baseline_program','history') and not re.fullmatch(r'trial/(?:[1-9]|10)/(?:proposal|report)',d['resource'])):raise ValueError('Unavailable resource')
    if d['tool']=='analyze' and (d['dataset'] not in ('train','selection') or d['view'] not in ('group_errors','target_bins','feature_error_correlation','readout_summary')):raise ValueError('Unavailable analysis')
    if d['tool']=='finish' and (not isinstance(d['conclusion'],str) or any(not isinstance(d[k],list) or any(not isinstance(x,str) for x in d[k]) for k in ('supported','not_supported'))):raise ValueError('Invalid final review')
    return d
